# .dockerignore
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PURPOSE: Tells Docker what NOT to copy into the image.
#          Everything listed here is excluded from COPY . . 
#
# WHY THIS MATTERS:
#   Without .dockerignore, COPY . . copies everything including
#   venv/ (1-2 GB), chroma_db/ (vector data), .env (secrets),
#   and data/ (your docx file) — making the image huge and insecure.
#
# RULE OF THUMB:
#   If it's not needed to RUN the app, exclude it.
#   Source code → include. Data, secrets, caches → exclude.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Python virtual environment ────────────────────────────────────────
# venv/ can be 1-2 GB. Container installs its own deps via requirements.txt
venv/
.venv/
env/

# ── Python cache files ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Bytecode cache — regenerated automatically, not needed in image
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.Python

# ── Secrets — NEVER bake into image ──────────────────────────────────
# .env contains API keys — if baked into image, anyone who pulls
# the image from ECR/DockerHub can read your API keys
.env
.env.*

# ── Vector database ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# chroma_db/ is mounted as a volume at runtime (docker-compose volumes)
# Baking it into the image means it can't be updated without rebuilding
# Also adds hundreds of MB to the image unnecessarily
# chroma_db/ included in image for AWS ECS deployment
# data/ included in image for AWS ECS deployment
# ── Source documents ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# data/ is mounted as a volume at runtime
# Baking documents into image = document changes require full rebuild
# data/ included in image for AWS ECS deployment
# ── Logs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Logs are written at runtime and mounted as volume
# No point including them in the image
logs/
*.log

# ── Git ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Git history not needed inside container
.git/
.gitignore

# ── Tests ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Test files not needed to run the production app
test_*.py
tests/

# ── Documentation ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
README.md
*.md

# ── IDE and OS files ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Docker files themselves ───────────────────────────────────────────
# No need to include Docker config inside the container
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
.dockerignore